                    },
                    "message": "We should log error if multiple chassis paths are found."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Add a check for chassisId being empty."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 62,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 63,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "We should only add this link only if object path that has `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.PCIeSwitch` also has `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.PCIeDevice`. And we should not populate PCIeDevice link in this function since any Chassis link related error would cause PCIeDevice link to be not populated as well."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 63,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Split the handler into getSwitchChassisLink() and getSwitchPCIeDeviceLink() so the two lookups are independent \u2014 a Chassis failure no longer blocks the PCIeDevice link. getSwitchPCIeDeviceLink() uses getDbusObject() to verify the path actually implements xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.PCIeDevice before populating the link."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 72,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Use sdbusplus::message::object_path operator /."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/fabric.hpp",
                    "line": 72,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
